      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Content Capture Version 2.</para>
          <para>The second and newer Content Capture takes a more focused and leaner approach to passing the view hierarchy from the application to a system intelligence service. The required information is mostly limited to text on screen and bounding boxes of these text nodes. This version of Content Capture is also significantly more efficient at resource usage and recommended to be the default one for various system intelligence services to use.</para>
          <para>When this version is returned by <see cref="P:Android.Views.ContentCaptures.ContentCaptureSession.ContentCaptureVersion" />, developers should use Version 2 APIs to report node lifecycle and property updates. Version 1 notification methods and <see cref="M:Android.Views.ContentCaptures.ContentCaptureSession.Flush" /> do not report events when the session is configured for Version 2. <see cref="M:Android.Views.ContentCaptures.ContentCaptureSession.NewViewStructure(Android.Views.View)" /> and <see cref="M:Android.Views.ContentCaptures.ContentCaptureSession.NewVirtualViewStructure(Android.Views.Autofill.AutofillId,System.Int64)" /> still create structures.</para>
          <para>Content Capture Version 2 APIs include <see cref="M:Android.Views.ContentCaptures.ContentCaptureSession.NotifyNodeAppearedOrChanged(Android.Views.Autofill.AutofillId,Android.Views.ContentCaptures.ContentCaptureNodeProperties)" /> and <see cref="M:Android.Views.ContentCaptures.ContentCaptureSession.NotifyNodeDisappeared(Android.Views.Autofill.AutofillId)" />.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/contentcapture/ContentCaptureSession#VERSION_2" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.view.contentcapture.ContentCaptureSession.VERSION_2</code>.</a></format></para>
          <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
        </summary>
